# Testing Rules

- Read the repository's test configuration before choosing commands.
- Add or update tests when behavior changes; do not rely only on manual inspection for critical logic.
- Test the smallest relevant scope first, then run broader checks when practical.
- Cover success, failure, boundary, loading, empty, authorization, and regression cases as applicable.
- For UI, verify accessibility and responsive behavior when affected.
- For APIs/data, verify validation, authorization, error handling, and data integrity.
- Never claim a test passed unless it actually ran and passed.
- If validation cannot be run, report the exact limitation.
